[{"_1":2},"llms/index",{"_3":4},"data","# Documentation\n\n- [Deploy from AWS Marketplace](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/aws-marketplace): Run a preconfigured Lamassu IoT instance on Amazon EC2.\n- [Deploy Lamassu](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/overview): Choose the operating model that fits your infrastructure and control requirements.\n- [Use Lamassu as SaaS](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/saas): Consume Lamassu as a managed service without operating your own infrastructure.\n- [Fastlane](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane): Bootstrap a complete Lamassu evaluation or lab environment on an existing Kubernetes cluster.\n- [Install with Helm](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/helm): Prepare dependencies, configure the Lamassu chart and verify a controlled Kubernetes deployment.\n- [Expose the Gateway](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/networking): Choose how clients reach Lamassu, when to set gateway.addresses and how to design multiple Gateways.\n- [Kubernetes self-managed](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/self-hosted/overview): Choose an installation workflow and network architecture for Lamassu on your Kubernetes cluster.\n- [Deployment troubleshooting](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/deployment/troubleshooting): Diagnose access, service health and infrastructure dependencies.\n- [Access control](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/administration/access-control): Design who can access Lamassu through principals, policies, resource permissions and HTTP route authorization.\n- [Alerts and subscriptions](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/administration/alerts): Send PKI events to people and external systems.\n- [Audit logs](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/administration/audit-logs): Understand which audit events Lamassu generates and how to turn them into a durable trail.\n- [Platform architecture](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/concepts/architecture): Lamassu components and how control, keys, issuance and devices relate.\n- [How Lamassu works](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/concepts/overview): The mental model of trust, keys, certificates and devices.\n- [Devices and identities](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/device-management): Register, inspect and retire devices while checking their current identity and history.\n- [Bootstrap identity and authentication](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/bootstrap-identity): Prepare server trust and admission proofs for enroll and reenroll.\n- [Configure and operate the DMS](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms): Define registration, authentication per operation, issuance, renewal and distributed trust.\n- [Integrate the EST client](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/est-client): Prepare trust, send a CSR and check the identity you receive.\n- [EST reference](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/est-reference): Look up Lamassu routes, formats, authentication and multipart responses.\n- [Enrollment with PKI](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/overview): Choose admission policy and connect DMS, initial trust and the EST client.\n- [Provisioning strategies](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/provisioning-strategies): Choose device registration, identity authorization and key generation.\n- [Renewal and recovery](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/renewal-and-recovery): Renew without losing the identity and recover devices according to their actual state.\n- [Enrollment troubleshooting](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting): Locate transport, authentication, registration, issuance and installation failures.\n- [Trust distribution and updates](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution): Separate roots, intermediates and initial TLS trust when distributing or migrating certificates.\n- [AWS IoT Core](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core): Lamassu's connector for AWS IoT Core syncs device identities with the AWS platform, handling CA registration, Thing provisioning and certificate lifecycle automatically and event-driven.\n- [IoT Fleets](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/overview): Organize devices and their identities, prepare enrollment and integrate consumers.\n- [Enroll and connect your first device](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device): Obtain an identity through EST, verify its association and use it in an mTLS connection.\n- [Register a device manually](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device): Prepare a DMS, register a device and associate a verified certificate with its identity.\n- [Lamassu IoT Platform](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/overview): Build a PKI and apply its certificates to your devices' lifecycle.\n- [CA hierarchy and rotation](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation): Design root and intermediate authorities and replace certificates or keys without breaking trust.\n- [Certification authorities](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/certificate-authorities): Create, import and operate the authorities that establish your PKI's trust.\n- [Certificate profiles](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/certificate-profiles): Define reusable policies to issue consistent certificates and constrain accepted keys.\n- [Certificate validation](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/certificate-validation): Check chain, identity, purpose and revocation from the consumer.\n- [Certificates](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/certificates): Inspect, download and revoke the certificates issued by Lamassu.\n- [Certificate lifecycle](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle): Issuance, use, renewal, revocation and retirement of certificates in Lamassu.\n- [Trust model](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model): Understand where trust originates, how it is distributed and what each component validates.\n- [Revocation lists (CRL)](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/crl): Generate and distribute signed lists to validate certificates offline.\n- [Keys and cryptographic engines](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/key-management): Generate, import and operate keys without coupling the PKI to a specific provider.\n- [Online validation with OCSP](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/ocsp): Query signed status and verify the responder’s response.\n- [PKI](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/overview): Administer keys and authorities, define issuance and verify the resulting certificates.\n- [Create your first CA](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority): Create an evaluation root and check its certificate before issuing.\n- [Issue and verify a certificate](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate): Issue a client certificate and check content, chain and key correspondence.\n- [PKI getting started](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview): Create a CA, issue a client certificate and check its chain and key.\n- [PKI troubleshooting](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/pki/troubleshooting): Diagnose certificate issuance, OCSP and CRL.\n- [Architecture](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/architecture): The components of Lamassu Updates, how they connect in each backend, and what runs in the background.\n- [Concepts](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/concepts): Update packs, software modules, launch campaigns, workflows and how an update reaches a device.\n- [Data model](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/data-model): The tables the service keeps, how they relate, and how the schema is created and migrated.\n- [Flows](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/flows): Sequence diagrams of the important operations, for the native and hawkBit backends.\n- [Get started with Lamassu Updates](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started): Run Lamassu Updates and its dependencies locally with Docker Compose and check that the API answers.\n- [Connect a device](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device): What a device must do to receive updates from Lamassu Updates, in native mode and in hawkBit mode.\n- [Use the dashboard](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/dashboard): Publish, roll out and follow an update from the Lamassu dashboard, screen by screen.\n- [Update flow with curl, hawkBit backend](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl): Every request of a complete update in hawkBit mode, including the device side over DDI, with real responses.\n- [Update flow with curl, native backend](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl): Every request of a complete update in native mode, from creating a pack to the last device, with real responses.\n- [Publish and roll out an update](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out): Create an update pack, attach an artifact, build the deliverable and roll it out to a device group in batches.\n- [hawkBit mode](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode): Run the same Lamassu Updates API on top of an Eclipse hawkBit server, what the adapter keeps in Postgres, and what differs from native mode.\n- [Limitations and known issues](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/limitations): What Lamassu Updates does not support or does not do yet, collected in one place with the page that explains each item.\n- [Operations](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/operations): Deploy Lamassu Updates with Docker Compose or Helm, scale it out, size it, observe it, back it up and upgrade it.\n- [Lamassu Updates](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/overview): What the service does, how it fits with Lamassu IoT, WFX and hawkBit, and where to start.\n- [API reference](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api): Every route of the Lamassu Updates and SymKMS HTTP APIs, with request bodies, status codes and per-backend behaviour.\n- [Capabilities](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities): The 22 capability flags of Lamassu Updates, what each backend supports, and how a client reads them.\n- [Configuration reference](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration): Every configuration key of Lamassu Updates, its default, which backend reads it, and how to override it with environment variables.\n- [Security](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security): What Lamassu Updates does and does not protect, and what to put around it before exposing it.\n- [Signing and encryption](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption): Sign deliverables with the Lamassu KMS, encrypt them with a shared or per-device key, and manage device keys in SymKMS.\n- [Troubleshooting](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting): Symptoms, likely causes and fixes for start-up errors, API calls, builds, downloads and updates that do not reach devices.\n- [3.8.0 to 4.0.0](/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/upgrades/3-8-0-to-4-0-0): What changes in the 4.0.0 architecture, which changes break a 3.8.0 deployment, how to upgrade a Helm release step by step and how to validate the result."]
